# Low Water, Act 1: interrogations (SYSTEMS-FULL section 20). Director, 2026-10-17.
# Live, on the plate: the person stays put and says their lies on their own clock; Lamb presses.
# Shape agreed with the systems engineer (NOTES-FOR-ENGINEER). Press nodes end with return:.

# ================================================================ Merrow, at the Brine stove
@interrogation x1.merrow
name: Merrow, about the drowned lamp
who: merrow
place: brine
nerve: 6
heat: 0
cool: 1
hold: 25
bolt: 5 -> x1.merrow.bolts
swing: 8 -> e.salvors
break: x1.merrow.tells
walk: x1.merrow.walk
press: fist "Take him by the collar, against the stove." -> x1.merrow.collar {nerve: -3, heat: +3, skill: grip, dc: 5}
press: tongue "Ask what the Low Company lost when the copper went." -> x1.merrow.lost {nerve: -2, heat: -1, skill: condolence, dc: 5}
press: hands "Put his copper sack on the bench between you." -> x1.merrow.sack ? count(i.copper_sack) > 0 {nerve: -4}
press: shadow "Tell him where his prints go on the floor." -> x1.merrow.prints ? has(prints.read) {nerve: -4}
press: any "Say nothing, and wait." -> x1.merrow.wait {nerve: -1, again}
lie: l.boat "Never left the boat. Not tonight." {catch: merrow.wet_thigh, nerve: -4, node: x1.merrow.caught, after: 5}
tell: 3 "He stops turning the cold pipe in his hands."

@node x1.merrow.start
place: brine
speaker: MERROW
cost: 1
nar: Merrow does not turn round. The steam comes off his trousers in a slow sheet.
line: Ask, then. I'm warm, for now.
do: interrogate(x1.merrow)
return:

@node x1.merrow.collar
speaker: MERROW
line: Get your hand off. That's my good coat. My only one.
return:

@node x1.merrow.lost
speaker: MERROW
line: Copper's what keeps a boat up the beach in winter. You'd not know. You're paid by the year.
return:

@node x1.merrow.sack
speaker: MERROW
nar: He looks at the sack a long time, the way a man looks at a dog that went missing.
line: That's not wreckers' work. That's mine. Was mine.
return:

@node x1.merrow.prints
speaker: MERROW
line: Anybody can walk on the floor. It's the floor.
nar: He says it to the stove.
return:

@node x1.merrow.wait
nar: The fire ticks. Somebody at the bar laughs at something else.
return:

@node x1.merrow.caught
speaker: MERROW
nar: The Damp's line on his trousers is a hand above the knee. He sees the assessor see it.
line: All right. All right, then.
return:

@node x1.merrow.tells
place: brine
speaker: MERROW
cost: 6
do: set(merrow.light); set(merrow.told); quest(a1.lowlight, merrow)
line: I was in the hole with a lantern, for the copper. Knocked it out climbing in, at eighteen past. Lit it again at twenty-five past.
line: In between, it was dark in there. I'd know. I was in it.
nar: He knocks the cold pipe out on the stove, though there is nothing in it.
go: brine.hub

@node x1.merrow.bolts
place: brine
speaker: MERROW
cost: 2
line: I'm going out to my boat. Come and ask the boat.
nar: The yard door bangs. The steam stays where he was standing.
go: brine.hub

@node x1.merrow.walk
speaker: MERROW
line: That's right. Go on.
go: brine.hub

# ================================================================ Marrow, in the Guild hall
@interrogation x1.marrow
name: Marrow Dunlin, about the switch
who: marrow
place: hall
nerve: 7
heat: 1
cool: 1
bolt: 9 -> x1.marrow.walk
swing: 6 -> e.afterdark
break: x1.marrow.tells
walk: x1.marrow.walk
press: fist "Lean on the pans till the beam tips." -> x1.marrow.pans {nerve: -2, heat: +3, skill: ballast, dc: 6}
press: tongue "Ask about his father, and the switch that was never for the sea." -> x1.marrow.father ? has(heard.marrow.father) {nerve: -3, heat: -1, skill: condolence, dc: 6}
press: hands "Lay the scales from the switch handle on the long table." -> x1.marrow.scales ? has(scales.kept) {nerve: -4}
press: shadow "Repeat what he told Shadwell at the fire-door." -> x1.marrow.door ? has(afterdark.told) {nerve: -4}
press: any "Let the hall hear the question." -> x1.marrow.hall {nerve: -1, heat: +1}
lie: l.switch "Nobody in this hall touched the Municipal's switch." {catch: scales.switch, nerve: -4, node: x1.marrow.caught, after: 6}
tell: 3 "The big hands go flat on the table."

@node x1.marrow.start
place: hall
speaker: MARROW
cost: 1
nar: The hall goes quiet in the order people notice: the near end first, then the pans, then the door.
line: Go on, flatfish. Say it in here.
do: interrogate(x1.marrow)
return:

@node x1.marrow.pans
speaker: MARROW
line: Take your weight off the Guild's pans before I take it off for you.
return:

@node x1.marrow.father
speaker: MARROW
nar: He looks at the Captain's apron under its glass, and not at the assessor.
line: Thirty years that switch went down, and nothing went with it but our lamps.
return:

@node x1.marrow.scales
speaker: MARROW
line: Herring scales. Half Gullet's got herring scales on it.
nar: Nobody in the hall laughs.
return:

@node x1.marrow.door
speaker: MARROW
line: Shadwell's door talks too much. Like Shadwell.
return:

@node x1.marrow.hall
nar: Somebody at the back says the Captain's name, low. Somebody else tells him to shut it.
return:

@node x1.marrow.caught
speaker: MARROW
line: Scales on the handle. Aye. Mine.
return:

@node x1.marrow.tells
place: hall
speaker: MARROW
cost: 6
do: set(marrow.switch)
line: I pulled it. Twenty to ten, the way my father did, for the vote. The quay went dark, and the vote went on in the dark, by the nose.
line: I didn't look down the mole first. He always looked. I didn't.
nar: The pans turn on their hooks, a little, in a draught nobody can feel.
go: gut.hall.menu

@node x1.marrow.walk
speaker: MARROW
line: Door's where you came in.
go: gut.hub

# ================================================================ Wenna, at the Brine fire
@interrogation x1.wenna
name: Wenna, about twenty to ten
who: wenna
place: brine
nerve: 8
heat: 0
cool: 1
hold: 30
bolt: 3 -> x1.wenna.bolts
break: x1.wenna.tells
walk: x1.wenna.walk
press: fist "Stand over her chair." -> x1.wenna.over {nerve: -1, heat: +3}
press: tongue "Talk about the stairs, and the knees, and twenty-eight years." -> x1.wenna.years {nerve: -3, heat: -1, skill: condolence, dc: 6}
press: hands "Open the log at tonight's page and lay it on her knee." -> x1.wenna.log ? has(log.ahead) {nerve: -4}
press: shadow "Ask what she heard at twenty to ten that made her lift her head." -> x1.wenna.motor ? has(wenna.heard_motor) {nerve: -4}
press: eye "Look at her coat, which is dry." -> x1.wenna.coat ? has(coat.wenna_dry) {nerve: -2}
lie: l.panel "I was at the panel. Where else would I be." {catch: log.ahead, nerve: -4, node: x1.wenna.caught, after: 6}
tell: 4 "She holds her cup in both hands and does not drink."

@node x1.wenna.start
place: brine
speaker: WENNA
cost: 1
nar: Wenna has the chair nearest the fire, and her oilskin over Jory's peg, as if it had always been there.
line: You'll be wanting to know where I was. Everybody does, tonight.
do: interrogate(x1.wenna)
return:

@node x1.wenna.over
speaker: WENNA
line: I've had men stand over me. Bigger than you. In better hats.
return:

@node x1.wenna.years
speaker: WENNA
line: A hundred and twelve. Twice a night for twenty-eight years. You count them even when you don't want to.
return:

@node x1.wenna.log
speaker: WENNA
nar: She looks at her own hand on the page: the line for half past ten, written before half past ten.
return:

@node x1.wenna.motor
speaker: WENNA
line: A car. On the hill road. Nobody drives the hill road at night but the one person.
return:

@node x1.wenna.coat
speaker: WENNA
line: It's a good coat. It keeps the rain off. That's what coats are for.
return:

@node x1.wenna.caught
speaker: WENNA
line: No. I wasn't.
return:

@node x1.wenna.tells
place: brine
speaker: WENNA
cost: 6
do: set(wenna.told_landing)
line: I was on the landing at fifty-six. On the chair. My knees wouldn't do the rest, and I sat, and I heard the motor, and I sat.
line: Six years nobody's paid me to climb. I climb anyway. Tonight I didn't.
go: brine.hub

@node x1.wenna.bolts
place: brine
speaker: WENNA
cost: 2
line: I'll sit somewhere I'm not stood over.
nar: She takes her cup to the far end of the bar, and her back says the rest.
go: brine.hub

@node x1.wenna.walk
speaker: WENNA
line: That's right. Leave an old woman to her fire.
go: brine.hub

# ================================================================ Hobb, at the weigh-house door
@interrogation x1.hobb
name: Constant Hobb, about the quay board
who: hobb
place: weigh_out
nerve: 4
heat: 0
cool: 1
bolt: 3 -> x1.hobb.bolts
break: x1.hobb.tells
walk: x1.hobb.walk
press: fist "Step close, and take the pencil out of his hand." -> x1.hobb.pencil {nerve: -2, heat: +3}
press: tongue "Tell him, in the Board's own words, that he will not be blamed." -> x1.hobb.blamed {nerve: -2, skill: formletter, dc: 5}
press: hands "Open Gorm's book at tonight's round, under his nose." -> x1.hobb.book ? has(quay.round.known) {nerve: -3}
press: shadow "Tell him where he was standing at twenty to ten." -> x1.hobb.standing {nerve: -2}
lie: l.nobody "Nobody past, assessor. Nobody went near the board." {catch: scales.switch, nerve: -3, node: x1.hobb.caught, after: 4}
tell: 2 "He writes the time down, and then the time again."

@node x1.hobb.start
place: weigh_out
speaker: HOBB
cost: 1
line: I've to write you down, assessor. It isn't personal. Everybody.
do: interrogate(x1.hobb)
return:

@node x1.hobb.pencil
speaker: HOBB
line: That's Municipal property, that pencil. I'll have to write that down. With what, I don't know.
return:

@node x1.hobb.blamed
speaker: HOBB
line: In writing? You'd put it in writing? Nobody's ever put anything in writing for me.
return:

@node x1.hobb.book
speaker: HOBB
line: That's the sergeant's book. I'm not to look in the sergeant's book. I'm looking.
return:

@node x1.hobb.standing
speaker: HOBB
line: By the board. I'm always by the board. That's my standing place.
return:

@node x1.hobb.caught
speaker: HOBB
line: I'm not to say. I've said I'm not to say. That's nearly saying.
return:

@node x1.hobb.tells
place: weigh_out
speaker: HOBB
cost: 4
do: set(weigh.hobb_saw)
line: Mr Dunlin. He put his hand on the switch like it was a dog's head, and pulled it, and the quay went out.
line: I wrote it down. I don't know what to write it down as.
go: weigh.hub

@node x1.hobb.bolts
place: weigh_out
speaker: HOBB
cost: 2
line: I've to take this to the sergeant. I'm sorry, assessor. I'll walk slowly.
go: weigh.hub

@node x1.hobb.walk
speaker: HOBB
line: Right. I'll put you down as going.
go: weigh.hub
